  "holistic_F_H": -2,
  "section_notes": "S1 requires mandatory reporting of serious incidents within 24 hours and other confirmed overheating incidents requiring emergency response or out-of-service within 5 business days, but excludes minor incidents (serious-only scope). S2 sets a 55°C test and 5% benchmark, provides complete results to customers but not public, allows corrective action instead of automatic ban, and does not explicitly require retesting existing models. S3 requires remote shut-off on new models after 24 months and retrofit within 72 months; S4 requires built-in fire suppression after 36 months; S5 mandates recall at 8 incidents per 100k with immediate customer notice, but lacks a serious-injury recall clause."
